  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "`channel` cannot be removed because it is still required downstream by **`analytics-ingest`** (team Data):\n\n1. **Downstream contract requirement:**\n   - In [`analytics-ingest/README.md`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/README.md#L26-L33), the contract for [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) explicitly requires `channel` (`web|store|marketplace`).\n   - [`decodeOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L25-L46) in [events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L34) reads and validates `channel`:\n     ```ts\n     const channel = reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS);\n     ```\n   - In [ingest.ts](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts#L17), the field is written into the lake's `orders` table as [`OrderRow`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/rows.ts#L6-L12).\n2. **Breaking change impact:**\n   - Missing `channel` triggers [`ContractViolationError`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/errors.ts#L14-L23), causing `analytics-ingest` to reject the entire event and drop all rows for that order (tested in [ingest.test.ts](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts#L88-L90)).\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\nBefore removing `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) and [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) in `orders-service`, the consumer repository `analytics-ingest` must first migrate its contract and lake table schema to stop requiring `channel`.\n",
